79097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":7,"created_at":"2026-04-03T21:49:12Z","updated_at":"2026-04-07T15:57:56Z","closed_at":"2026-04-07T15:45:00Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118170","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118170","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118170.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118170.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"# Problem\r\nThe `JSON::parse` function will parse all numbers as a `double`. This makes rendering strings difficult for me since I rely on the JSON result to tell me the schema. I don't want a value like `{\"number\":5}` rendered as `5.0` instead it should be `5`.\r\n\r\n# Example\r\n\r\n```gd\r\nvar res = JSON.parse_string(\"5\")\r\nprint(res) # prints 5.0 instead of 5\r\n```\r\n\r\n# Solution\r\nI changed the code so that it will output an `int` result if a number is missing the `.`, `e` or `E` character otherwise it falls back to its original behavior of parsing as a double. ","closed_by":{"login":"mashumafi","id":1059099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTkwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1059099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mashumafi","html_url":"https://github.com/mashumafi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mashumafi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mashumafi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mashumafi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mashumafi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url